<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lismore, County Waterford</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lismore is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-waterford">County Waterford</a>, Ireland, on the River Blackwater. Saint Carthach, also called Mochuda, founded a monastery there in the 7th century that became one of the leading centres of learning in early medieval Ireland and the seat of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>. The town is dominated by Lismore Castle, and the late medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> known as the Book of Lismore takes its name from it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lismore-county-waterford.jpg" alt="Lismore, County Waterford" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: https://www.geograph.org.uk/profile/10423 Mike Searle] · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castles_of_Munster,_Lismore,_Waterford-geograph-3038250.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
